Data source in the code
=======================

src/u6-extractors-workload/root-zone-tlds.ts (compiled into dist/) holds the list of top-level domains of the DNS
root zone, lower-cased, from the registry's file https://data.iana.org/TLD/tlds-alpha-by-domain.txt, version line
"Version 2026111500, Last Updated Sun Nov 15 07:07:01 2026 UTC", read on 2026-11-15 (docs/lookups.md). It is a
factual registry list; the file states no licence. crankpath uses it to decide whether a two-label host name can be
a public name.

Third-party files in the source repository
==========================================

The source repository (not the npm package) holds trimmed copies of four public GitOps estates as test data, under
test/corpus/<folder>/repo/. crankpath scans them in its tests to check that it handles real estates; they are never
applied to a cluster. Each folder holds the upstream licence text copied unchanged as LICENSE and a NOTICE giving the
origin, the commit, the date of the copy and what was trimmed; corpus.json lists every copied file with its SHA-256.
The folder, origin, commit and licence of each, checked against its LICENSE text on 2026-11-16:

  test/corpus/flux2-kustomize-helm-example/
      https://github.com/fluxcd/flux2-kustomize-helm-example
      commit 4f1a5b1051b469108d1bdf0ebec6c814427e3834   Apache-2.0

  test/corpus/gitops-bridge-control-plane-template/
      https://github.com/gitops-bridge-dev/gitops-bridge-argocd-control-plane-template
      commit e6d355197ff3af8e6be09e1dea068dc12727a915   Apache-2.0

  test/corpus/acelinkio-argocd-homelab/
      https://github.com/acelinkio/argocd-homelab
      commit 2f9aab023f92b6d73051bd86ec163a48a56dbe1e   MIT (Copyright (c) 2023 acelinkio)

  test/corpus/bjw-s-home-ops/
      https://github.com/bjw-s-labs/home-ops
      commit e6e44645283b5e138d5f4faa2e83e028947c702b   Apache-2.0

Every copied file is byte-identical to the upstream file at that commit: the copies are trimmed by leaving files out,
never by editing one, so no file carries a "Modified by crankpath" line (section 4(b) of the Apache License asks for
one on a modified file). None of the four upstream repositories has a NOTICE file to carry forward (section 4(d)):
checked in each clone at the copied commit on 2026-11-16. Apache-2.0 and MIT files may be distributed with a work
licensed under Apache-2.0 provided their licence is kept with them; it is kept beside each copy. Nothing in a corpus
folder is relicensed: the files under repo/ stay under their upstream licence, and only corpus.json, expected.json and
NOTICE in each folder are crankpath's own work.

Dependencies installed from the npm registry (commander, yaml and the development tools) are not copied into this
repository or into the package; their licences are in package-lock.json and in docs/lookups.md.
